course: dictionary
lesson: 14689
title: The twisted word: pretzel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pretzel is a baked snack made from dough twisted into a loose knot shape. It is usually salty. «She bought a bag of pretzels at the fair.» Pretzels can be hard and crunchy, or big and soft.
explain: The word can also be used in a playful way. «He twisted himself into a pretzel to fit under the table.» Here it does not mean a snack. It is an informal word for something bent or twisted into a strange shape, like a person's body.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. If the sentence is about eating, buying or counting snacks, it is the food. If it is about a person or thing bent into a shape, it is the informal meaning.
fact: A pretzel is a baked snack made from dough.
fact: Pretzels are usually salty and have a loose knot shape.
fact: Pretzels can be hard and crunchy, or big and soft.
fact: Pretzels are popular in Germany and are common in the USA.
fact: «Pretzel sticks» are thin, and «a soft pretzel» is a bigger, softer snack.
fact: Informal: «twisted like a pretzel» means bent into a strange shape.
exercise: How many pretzels are left in «A bag holds 12 pretzels. Sam eats 4»? | *8 | 16 | 4 | 6
exercise: What is a pretzel? | A soft blanket | *A baked snack made from dough twisted into a loose knot | A small red fruit | A fast kind of bus
exercise: «He twisted himself into a pretzel to fit under the bed.» What does pretzel mean here? | A type of bread for lunch | A small dog | *Something bent or twisted into a strange shape | A salty snack
test: What shape is a pretzel? | A straight stick | *A loose knot | A flat circle with no holes | A square box
test: Pretzels are a popular snack from which country? | Japan | Italy | Egypt | *Germany
exam: «Ella ate 3 pretzels from a bag of 10.» How many pretzels were left in the bag? | 3 | 13 | 6 | *7
